WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.542
JENNY BROWN: This
week, we're talking

00:00:01.542 --> 00:00:04.770
about the newest Google Cloud
region, hybrid connectivity,

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:07.470
and the 2020 IT skills survey.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:10.260
I'm Jenny Brown, and welcome
to "This Week in Cloud," where

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:13.770
we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:16.379
Our CEO recently announced
a new partnership

00:00:16.379 --> 00:00:18.870
with Poland's domestic
cloud provider.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:20.430
As a part of that
partnership, we're

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:23.340
opening a brand new Google
Cloud region in Warsaw

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.680
to bring lower latency
and higher performance

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.230
to Central and Eastern Europe.

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:31.650
Cloud computing solutions depend
on great networks as well as

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:32.820
great products.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:34.980
And to help you make
your network the best,

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:37.140
we've graduated two
services from beta

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:39.000
to general availability.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.940
100 Gigabits-per-second
Dedicated Interconnect

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:44.160
can scale your
connection capacity,

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:46.320
and High-Availability
VPN protects

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:50.910
your mission-critical workloads
with an industry-leading 99.99%

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:52.280
SLA.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:56.310
The Global Knowledge 2019
IT Skills and Salary Report

00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:59.310
gave us a comprehensive
look at industry standards,

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:01.650
certifications,
and compensation,

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:03.480
all broken down by region.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:06.480
The 2020 survey is running
now through November 8.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:09.150
So if you're an IT professional
and have about 10 minutes

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.340
to spare, we'd love
to hear your voice

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:15.450
in the largest worldwide study
of the growing IT industry.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:18.700
Machine learning is all anyone
can talk about these days.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:21.420
But if your co-workers
keep throwing ML and AI

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:23.400
around interchangeably,
please feel

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:26.130
free to direct them to
this lovely ML breakdown

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:28.650
brought to you by the
Google Comics Factory.

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:30.600
It's got everything
you need to learn--

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:33.600
solid examples, clear
expectations, and of course,

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:35.340
cartoon cats.

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:37.440
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:40.180
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:41.500
Have thoughts or ideas?

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:45.230
Leave us a comment or tweet us,
and we'll see you in the cloud.

